---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Base title="About | Freelancer Stack" description="Why Freelancer Stack exists, how we choose software, and how we make money.">
  <PageHero
    label="About"
    title="Software advice without the sales pitch."
    lede="Freelancer Stack is for people who work for themselves and would rather spend their money on rent than on software they barely use."
  />

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>Search "best invoicing software" and you get lists where every tool is "great for everyone" and the top pick pays the biggest commission. That is not advice. It is an ad wearing a cardigan.</p>
      <p>Freelancers deserve better than that. When you work for yourself, every subscription comes out of your own pocket, and every hour spent wrestling with a tool is an hour you can't bill. Picking the wrong one costs twice.</p>
      <p>So we built the guide we wanted: short, plain, and honest about who should <em>not</em> buy something.</p>

      <h2>What we believe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Less is more.</strong> Most freelancers need four jobs done: win the client, book the work, track the time, get paid. Anything beyond that has to earn its place.</li>
        <li><strong>Free is often enough.</strong> If a free plan does the job, we say so, even when it earns us nothing.</li>
        <li><strong>Fees matter more than prices.</strong> A cheap tool with high payment fees can cost more than an expensive one. We look at the whole bill.</li>
        <li><strong>"It depends" is a real answer.</strong> We tell you what it depends on.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>We check prices and features on each vendor's own website and note the date we checked. Where we've used a tool ourselves, we tell you what it was like. Where we haven't, we say that too, rather than pretending.</p>
      <p>We update guides when tools change. If you spot something out of date, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and we'll fix it.</p>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you sign up through one, the company may pay us a commission at no extra cost to you. That's what keeps the site free and independent. It never decides what we recommend, and we never take payment to rank a tool. <a href="/disclosure/">Read the full disclosure</a>.</p>

      <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
      <p class="placeholder">To do: add the real person (or people) behind the site: name, what you do, and why you care about freelancer tools. A real face builds more trust than any logo.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
